// CORRECT - look for patterns across ALL failing tests first
```

## Forbidden Practices (NEVER DO) - Phase 1 Test Suite 3 Additions

### ❌ Never Create Test Files with Raw Malicious Paths
```javascript
// WRONG - causes ENOENT filesystem errors
const tempFilePath = path.join(tempDir, '../../../etc/passwd');
fs.writeFileSync(tempFilePath, content); // Fails with ENOENT

// CORRECT - sanitize in helper function
const safeFilename = filename.replace(/[\/\\]/g, '_').replace(/\.\./g, '__');
const tempFilePath = path.join(tempDir, safeFilename);
```

### ❌ Never Confuse HTTP-Level and Content-Level Validation
```javascript
// WRONG - expecting fileFilter to reject based on content
const pngContent = '\x89PNG\r\n\x1a\n'; 
createTestFile(pngContent, 'fake.json'); // Still passes fileFilter (correct .json extension)

// CORRECT - test appropriate validation layer
// Test fileFilter with unsupported extensions (.exe, .sh)
// Test content validation with invalid content in valid extensions
```

## Forbidden Practices (NEVER DO) - Phase 1 Test Suite 4 Additions

### ❌ Never Add user_id After Validation in Import Services
```javascript
// WRONG - causes validation failures because user_id is required
const validatedItem = validateData(processedItem, schema); // Fails: user_id required
validatedItem.user_id = userId; // Too late

// CORRECT - add user_id before validation
processedItem.user_id = userId;
const validatedItem = validateData(processedItem, schema); // Passes: user_id present
```

